abstract: >-
  The Luddite-fallacy claim about aggregate unemployment still holds in U.S. and
  Western official data through mid-2026. The Ricardo–Acemoglu–Restrepo claim
  about task displacement, labor’s share of income, and which cohorts lose the
  hiring channel is the part that is moving. Version 1.2 is the Zenodo version of
  record. It adds a Western comparison and states the claim as a testable
  identity—the Displacement–Redundancy Balance—with two monitoring statistics,
  the canary residual and the wage-fund conversion ratio, that later vintages
  can reshape.
